      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/k/d26b3c/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2012-05-13T16:22:14.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p><a class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/josul0215\">@josul0215</a>: Actually, it is; if a creatures toughness is reduced to zero, it’s placed in the graveyard as a state-based effect, such that regeneration and the like will not trigger on its demise. It’s not destroyed, like it would be from combat damage (that isn’t from a creature with infect) or by (most) spells.</p>",
